2.2 The Six Safety Guarantees
1. No Hallucination — The system cannot generate outputs outside its ROM-defined
knowledge. It can only return 0x-AMBIG ("I don't know").
2. Deterministic Output — Same input → same output. Always. No variation. No drift.
3. Formal Verifiability — The FSM is proven against safety properties via TLA+
specifications.
4. Bounded Execution — Assured Execution Time (AET) ≤ 800 ns. Not a worst-case bound.
A physically assured constant.
5. Energy Sovereignty — 3.7 μJ per query. Passive cooling. No grid dependency. No data
center heat.
6. Air-Gappable — No cloud dependency. No API calls. No external control. Fully sovereign.
2.3 The Agentic Extension
ST-T1024 is not merely an inference primitive. The agentic extension (A0–A16) adds a
complete, formally verified action pipeline:
· A0 — FSM action pipeline, ROM-burned action library, VERIFY gate
· A2 — Action library schema: finite, enumerable, provable before deployment
· A11 — Agent Certificate: identity, authority, and capability declaration
· A12 — Intent Envelope: the bounded domain within which the agent may act
· A13 — Admission Protocol: gatekeeping for inter-organizational action
· A14 — Action Vocabulary Mapping: high-level intents to concrete actions
· A15 — Refusal as Wire Protocol: 0x-AMBIG elevated to a first-class, contractually
meaningful message
· A16 — Cross-Organizational Trace Ledger: append-only, hash-chained, independently
verifiable record of every action, refusal, and assumption-check The system is certifiable in principle because its complete behavior set is finite, enumerable,
and provable before deployment. A TLA+ suite verifies seven formal invariants: Safety,
Determinism, Timing, Isolation, Termination, Auditability, and Sovereignty.
